00:17:07,774 --> 00:17:10,896
他说这简直是对司机的赤裸裸税收，
and he says
it's a blatant tax on the motorist,

279
00:17:10,971 --> 00:17:15,025
他正要把斯温登所有的测速摄像头全部拆掉。
and he's getting rid of every speed camera
in Swindon.

280
00:17:15,101 --> 00:17:16,929
哦，是吧！
Oh, yeah!

281
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:19,862
起立鼓掌，Peter Greenhalgh。
Standing ovation, Peter Greenhalgh.

282
00:17:19,932 --> 00:17:24,827
女士们先生们，我们得给他致敬，不能让这个时刻就这么溜走。
Ladies and gentlemen, we have to honor him,
we can't just let this moment pass.

283
00:17:25,195 --> 00:17:31,215
不行。官方利益登记册上写明，他没有接受任何礼物或招待。
No. In the official register of interest, it says
he hasn't accepted any gifts or hospitality.

284
00:17:31,291 --> 00:17:34,743
好，那马上就改——因为我们给他准备了这个——
Well, that's gonna change right now
because we have this for him -

285
00:17:34,822 --> 00:17:39,547
这是《Top Gear》卓越奖杯，表彰他对常识的贡献，
it is the Top Gear trophy of excellence
for services to common sense,

286
00:17:39,619 --> 00:17:41,208
而它就是你的，Greenhalgh 先生。
and it is yours, Mr. Greenhalgh.

287
00:17:41,284 --> 00:17:45,111
在赤裸裸的政府蠢事面前，对常识的贡献。
Services to common sense in the face
of blatant government stupidity.

288
00:17:45,181 --> 00:17:48,236
如果你想在这里抢个座儿，我们甚至已经给你准备好椅子了。
If you want to pop up here and get that,
we've even provided you a chair.

289
00:17:48,313 --> 00:17:51,572
这是《Top Gear》感恩王座。
It is the Top Gear throne of gratitude.

290
00:17:54,509 --> 00:17:55,871
献给你，献给你。
For you, for you.

291
00:17:55,941 --> 00:17:59,837
Peter，你来到这里，这把椅子就是你的，永久归你。
Peter, you come here, that is your chair,
permanently here.

292
00:17:59,904 --> 00:18:01,801
真是个男人！
What a man!

293
00:18:01,870 --> 00:18:03,426
我想说一句，
Can I just say though,

294
00:18:03,502 --> 00:18:07,864
如果你以后几周住在、或者要开车穿过斯温顿，
if you do live in, or are gonna drive
through Swindon over the next few weeks,

295
00:18:07,933 --> 00:18:10,420
大家都会盯着看它到底行不行，
they're all gonna be watching
to see if it works,

296
00:18:10,498 --> 00:18:12,860
所以，拜托小心点。
so, please, be careful.

297
00:18:12,930 --> 00:18:16,689
如果你真在斯温顿出了点岔子，
If you do happen to have
any sort of accident in Swindon,

298
00:18:16,760 --> 00:18:20,054
等天黑了，把残骸推到德维兹去，
wait until it's dark
and push the wreckage into Devizes,

299
00:18:20,124 --> 00:18:23,884
然后装作被测速摄像头撞了。
and then claim you hit a speed camera.

300
00:18:23,955 --> 00:18:27,147
现在，克莱斯勒快要宣布，他们全系车子，
Now, Chrysler are about to announce
that all their cars across their range,

301
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:29,081
都将配备 Wi‑Fi 连接功能。
will come with wi-fi connectivity.

302
00:18:29,151 --> 00:18:30,446
呃？
Eh?

303
00:18:30,517 --> 00:18:34,708
对，你在后备箱里装个装置，随时随地连上网。
Yeah, you get a device in the boot that allows
you to hook up to the internet on the move.

304
00:18:34,781 --> 00:18:37,677
- 真是高大上。  
- 什么，你能查邮件吗？
- It's very clever.
- What, you'd be able to check your emails?

305
00:18:37,746 --> 00:18:38,972
对。
Yeah.

306
00:18:39,045 --> 00:18:41,736
你能去看看 Abi Titmus 那位女士的花园吗？
Would you be able to look at
Abi Titmus's lady garden?

307
00:18:41,810 --> 00:18:44,331
他们说这只给乘客用。
They do say it's for passengers only.

308
00:18:44,408 --> 00:18:49,393
这简直是那种‘我这周在 M40 上看到的奇葩。’
It really will be a case of "I went on
the M40 this week and I found this."

309
00:18:52,070 --> 00:18:53,228
你得这么干。
You had to.

310
00:18:55,267 --> 00:18:59,788
如果你想花二万五千镑左右买辆舒适、装备齐全的四座车，
Now, if you want a comfortable, well-equipped
four-seater for around £25,000,

311
00:18:59,864 --> 00:19:03,259
市面上已经有三十种不同车型。
there are currently 30 different models
on the market.

312
00:19:03,328 --> 00:19:07,348
但这俩胆大又怪异的家伙，觉得没有一款够格，
But these two, being bold and odd,
decided none of them were good enough,

313
00:19:07,426 --> 00:19:10,618
于是直接想买历史书里的车。
and instead they wanted to buy cars
from the pages of history.

314
00:19:10,690 --> 00:19:13,086
我得强调，接下来要说的，
Now, I should stress
that what we've got coming up now,

315
00:19:13,155 --> 00:19:15,813
可不是《Top Gear》那套常规的廉价车挑战，
isn't the usual Top Gear
cheap car challenge,

316
00:19:15,887 --> 00:19:19,941
因为这真的是他们的车，那些蠢…
because these really are their cars,
the stupid tw...

317
00:19:24,081 --> 00:19:25,478
这就是我买的。
This is what I've bought.

318
00:19:25,546 --> 00:19:31,566
它是 1972 年的 Rolls‑Royce Corniche 固定顶，车身由 H.J. Mulliner Park Ward 打造，
It's a 1972 Rolls-Royce Corniche fixed head
with coachwork by H.J. Mulliner Park Ward,

319
00:19:31,642 --> 00:19:34,834
它具备我在经典豪车里寻求的一切——
and it's everything I look for
in a classic luxury car -

320
00:19:34,907 --> 00:19:39,801
安静、极其舒适，而且彻头彻尾的英伦风。
it's quiet, it's supremely comfortable
and it's quintessentially British.

321
00:19:39,870 --> 00:19:43,925
坦白说，如果你有两万五千镑要花在经典豪车上，却不买这款…
Frankly, if you have £25,000 to spend on classic
luxury and you don't buy one of these...

322
00:19:44,967 --> 00:19:46,159
那你就是个蠢货。
you're an imbecile.

323
00:19:47,931 --> 00:19:49,986
明白我的意思吧？
See what I mean?

324
00:19:50,929 --> 00:19:53,189
戈林元帅来了。
Reich Marshal Goering has arrived.

325
00:19:53,261 --> 00:19:55,021
早上好。
Guten morgen.

326
00:19:55,093 --> 00:19:58,817
詹姆斯，你应该知道，这可是奔驰600古斯特尔，
This, James, as I'm sure you know,
is a Mercedes 600 Grosser,

327
00:19:58,890 --> 00:20:03,547
在1963年，它是世界上最贵的车。
which was, in 1963,
the most expensive car in the world.

328
00:20:03,620 --> 00:20:06,449
- 那时候就已经贵得离谱了，和大多数奔驰一样。
- 什么？才不是！
- Overpriced then, like most Mercedes.
- What? No!

329
00:20:06,519 --> 00:20:09,676
你的车有液压天窗吗？
Does your car have a hydraulically operated
sunshine roof?

330
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:11,215
- 没有。
- 液压车窗？
- No.
- Hydraulic windows?

331
00:20:11,282 --> 00:20:12,576
- 没有。
- 液压座椅？
- No.
- Hydraulic seats?

332
00:20:12,648 --> 00:20:14,738
- 全都没有。
- 液压车门？液压后备箱盖？
- No. No.
- Hydraulic doors? Hydraulic boot lid?

333
00:20:14,813 --> 00:20:16,641
- 没有。
- 那好吧。
- No.
- Well, there you are.

334
00:20:16,711 --> 00:20:17,768
那就这么定了？
That's that then, is it?

335
00:20:17,844 --> 00:20:20,967
你只有一辆带镀Chrome前脸的福特齐菲尔，那就是你的全部。
You've just got a Ford Zephyr
with a chrome nose, that's all yours is.

336
00:20:21,042 --> 00:20:23,233
这是一辆定制的手工打造的车。
This is a coach-built, hand-built car.

337
00:20:23,307 --> 00:20:26,237
手工制作不过是暗示门随时会掉下来。
Hand-built is just another way of saying
the door will fall off.

338
00:20:26,305 --> 00:20:30,099
这到底叫啥——劳斯莱斯穆林纳·帕克沃德？
What's this called -
Rolls-Royce Mulliner Park Ward?

339
00:20:30,169 --> 00:20:31,793
H.J.穆林纳·帕克沃德。
H.J. Mulliner Park Ward.

340
00:20:31,868 --> 00:20:34,025
听起来像是水管工大会的名字。
It just sounds like a plumber's convention.

341
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,997
我能给你们演示点东西吗——可以吗？
Can I just show you something - may I?

342
00:20:36,065 --> 00:20:39,892
看看这小窗户——知道它们是干嘛的吧？
See these little windows here -
do you know what they're for?

343
00:20:39,962 --> 00:20:42,324
就是当你坐在后排，车窗打开时，
So that when you're in back
and the window is down,

344
00:20:42,394 --> 00:20:45,256
它能挡住风，别把头发吹乱。
this stops the draught
messing your hair up.

345
00:20:45,325 --> 00:20:47,846
还有这个你见过吗？你的车有这个吗？
And have you seen this as well?
Has your car got these?

346
00:20:47,924 --> 00:20:49,219
- 窗帘？
- 窗帘。
- Curtains?
- Curtains.

347
00:20:49,290 --> 00:20:51,447
不，这玩意儿是装在房车里的。
No, they go in caravans.

348
00:20:51,521 --> 00:20:52,816
- 准备好了吗？
- 好的。
- Are you ready for this?
- Yes.

349
00:20:52,887 --> 00:20:54,215
行，准备好没？
OK, ready?

350
00:20:55,985 --> 00:20:58,415
其实这太精彩了，我得承认，
That's brilliant, actually,
I have to concede that,

351
00:20:58,483 --> 00:21:01,243
因为我一直觉得最难的就是这个。
because what I've always found
really difficult is this.

352
00:21:05,245 --> 00:21:08,834
显然，这只能用Top Gear唯一的方式来解决。
Plainly, this had to be settled
in the only way Top Gear knows.

353
00:21:12,773 --> 00:21:15,999
于是我们直奔测试赛道。
So, we headed for the test track.

354
00:21:17,237 --> 00:21:23,688
这款古斯特尔巩固了奔驰在工程可靠性上的声誉。
What the Grosser did was cement Mercedes'
reputation for engineering integrity.

355
00:21:23,766 --> 00:21:26,457
我想唯一原因是他们没把车做成钻石
I think the only reason
they didn't make it out of diamonds

356
00:21:26,531 --> 00:21:28,961
因为钻石太脆弱、太易碎了。
is because they're too weak and brittle.

357
00:21:30,528 --> 00:21:32,050
还有，那乘坐感受。
And then, there's the ride.

358
00:21:33,593 --> 00:21:36,489
它能把路上的颠簸全部抹平。
It just completely irons out bumps.

359
00:21:37,523 --> 00:21:41,283
我敢肯定，詹姆斯坐在他的福特齐菲尔里也会这么说。
And James will be saying the same thing
in that Ford Zephyr of his, I know he will.

360
00:21:42,353 --> 00:21:47,146
绝对不容任何事破坏乘坐品质。
Absolutely nothing is allowed
to compromise the quality of the ride.

361
00:21:48,816 --> 00:21:52,371
事实上，我倒是愿意相信，若你在七十年代为劳斯莱斯工作，
In fact, I like to believe that if you
worked at Rolls-Royce in the 1970s,

362
00:21:52,447 --> 00:21:57,069
而且你要是用了“操控”或“运动感”这种词，
and you ever used a word
like "handling" or "sporty",

363
00:21:57,143 --> 00:21:58,141
你就会被干掉。
you'd have been fired.

364
00:22:00,241 --> 00:22:02,932
这车是给国家元首开的。
This was a car for heads of state.

365
00:22:03,006 --> 00:22:04,232
说实话，独裁者们才是目标。
Dictators, if I'm honest.

366
00:22:05,304 --> 00:22:10,324
拥有600的人几乎总能调动空军——
People who had a 600
almost always had access to an air force -

367
00:22:10,401 --> 00:22:14,194
这也是为什么没人敢改装——部分原因是它有全世界最响的喇叭，
that's why nobody carves it up - partly because
it's got the loudest horn in the world,

368
00:22:14,265 --> 00:22:18,127
还有我可以随时叫来空袭。
and also because
I can call on an air strike.

369
00:22:19,928 --> 00:22:23,551
在赛道上，制片们安排了一连串的测试。
At the track, our producers
had laid on a series of tests.

370
00:22:23,626 --> 00:22:27,419
首轮，毫不意外地，让斯提格老大上场。
The first, inevitably, involved Lord Stig.

371
00:22:27,789 --> 00:22:29,913
好啊，让我惊喜一下。
OK, surprise me.

372
00:22:30,954 --> 00:22:37,042
“看起来，斯提格现在正驾驶一辆1.1升的现代IIO，穿梭于障碍赛道。”
"As you can see, the Stig is currently driving
a 1.1 liter Hyundai IIO down a slalom."

373
00:22:37,116 --> 00:22:38,139
这可是i10。
It's an i10.

374
00:22:39,615 --> 00:22:41,909
有人说那是他自己的车。
Some say that's his own car.

375
00:22:41,980 --> 00:22:48,499
“你们得用更豪华、更高端的车去超越他的成绩。”
"You will attempt to beat his time in your
much more elaborate and sophisticated cars."

376
00:22:48,575 --> 00:22:51,471
他来了。这车真是光荣又高贵啊。
Here he comes.
That's a proud and noble car, that is.

377
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:54,266
斯提格的基准已经定好，接着劳斯莱斯先上场。
With the Stig's marker laid down,

378
00:22:54,338 --> 00:22:55,701
上吧！
the Rolls went first.

379
00:22:55,770 --> 00:22:57,099
要是这车戴了单片眼镜，眼镜现在早掉了。
Hit it!

380
00:22:59,035 --> 00:23:01,692
舰长，我抓不住她。
If this car had a monocle,
it would fall out now.

381
00:23:04,031 --> 00:23:05,496
哦！
I can't hold her, cap'n.

382
00:23:05,564 --> 00:23:06,892
这可不是多体面的表演。
Oh!

383
00:23:09,062 --> 00:23:11,185
干！
It's not a dignified spectacle, that.

384
00:23:14,124 --> 00:23:15,884
他在倒车！
Cock!

385
00:23:16,057 --> 00:23:18,215
这真是荒唐。
He's reversing!

386
00:23:19,788 --> 00:23:21,776
我要吐了！
This was ridiculous.

387
00:23:21,852 --> 00:23:23,976
好，现代用了24.46秒完成，而詹姆斯……
I'm gonna be sick!

388
00:23:25,617 --> 00:23:30,739
这可不行，兄弟。
OK, so the Hyundai did it in 24.46 seconds,
and James...

389
00:23:30,813 --> 00:23:32,142
我本来有充分理由相信绿色的Grosser会更好。
that's not good, mate.

390
00:23:33,645 --> 00:23:38,471
这就是我的秘密武器。
I had good reason to imagine
the green Grosser would do better.

391
00:23:38,541 --> 00:23:40,335
把它往下压，减震器内部压力会升高
This is my secret weapon.

392
00:23:40,407 --> 00:23:44,303
达到每平方英寸3000磅。
Pull it down and it increases the pressure
in the shock absorbers

393
00:23:44,371 --> 00:23:47,199
- 该死！  
- 正是该死！
to 3,000lbs per square inch.

394
00:23:47,269 --> 00:23:49,256
那感觉就像F1赛车在那奔跑。
- Cor!
- It is cor!

395
00:23:49,334 --> 00:23:51,924
其实并不是。
It'll be like an F1 racer going down there.

396
00:23:53,065 --> 00:23:54,552
不，它并不像我预想的那样笔直平坦。
It wasn't.

397
00:23:56,230 --> 00:23:59,160
不过，和劳斯不同的是，它的转弯半径竟比跑道宽度还小。
No, it's not quite as straight and level
as I might have hoped.

398
00:24:00,093 --> 00:24:04,784
这其实挺不错的。
But, unlike the Rolls, its turning circle
was less than the width of the runway.

399
00:24:04,857 --> 00:24:06,980
你得记住，如果你后座坐着独裁者，而恐怖分子出现，
That's quite good, actually.

400
00:24:08,221 --> 00:24:13,048
你......
You've gotta bear in mind, if you've got a
dictator in the back and terrorists come,

401
00:24:13,118 --> 00:24:14,481
得赶紧跑了。
you've gotta get away quickly.

402
00:24:17,181 --> 00:24:21,406
哎呀，这比慢慢船长快多了。
Ooh, that's a lot faster than Captain Slow.

403
00:24:22,444 --> 00:24:23,670
操！
Cock!

404
00:24:23,744 --> 00:24:28,571
好，梅赛德斯先拿下第一滴血，接下来该来点新挑战了。
So, with first blood to the Mercedes,
it was time for our next challenge.

405
00:24:29,706 --> 00:24:33,158
接下来，你们俩要来场四分之一英里直线加速赛。
"There will now be a quarter-mile drag race
between the two of you."

406
00:24:34,204 --> 00:24:37,225
但唯一的规定是，不能用发动机。
But it says the only thing is,
you aren't allowed to use your engines.

407
00:24:38,401 --> 00:24:41,523
- 为啥？
- 说明老车经常抛锚。
- Why?
- It says old cars break down a lot

408
00:24:41,598 --> 00:24:44,926
而且你得练练把它们推离危险的本领。
and you should get used to
pushing them out of harm's way.

409
00:24:44,997 --> 00:24:47,393
啥？四分之一英里推车赛？
What, a quarter-mile pushing race?

410
00:24:49,094 --> 00:24:52,285
光想这事儿我背都快扭了。
I've put my back out
just thinking about doing this.

411
00:24:52,358 --> 00:24:54,380
你就是想倒戈，快说走。
You're trying to get out of it.
Just say go.

412
00:24:54,457 --> 00:24:56,115
准备好了吗？
Are we ready?

413
00:25:10,379 --> 00:25:11,809
- 我动了。
- 我没动。
- I'm moving.
- I'm not.

414
00:25:11,877 --> 00:25:13,308
我已经抢先了。
I was already ahead.

415
00:25:13,377 --> 00:25:15,398
我的鞋子根本没抓地。
I've got no traction on these shoes.

416
00:25:15,475 --> 00:25:16,997
哎呀！
Oh!

417
00:25:17,075 --> 00:25:19,561
你那车到底多重？
How much does yours actually weigh?

418
00:25:19,639 --> 00:25:21,127
2.2吨。
2.2 tonnes.

419
00:25:21,205 --> 00:25:22,897
我这的2.8。
Mine's 2.8.

420
00:25:22,971 --> 00:25:25,094
等等，你快把我甩开了。
Hang on, you're getting ahead.

421
00:25:25,169 --> 00:25:28,599
天啊，这太疼了。
God, this is painful.

422
00:25:33,097 --> 00:25:36,356
我再也走不动了，我心脏病要犯了。
I can't go another inch.
I've had a heart attack.

423
00:25:36,428 --> 00:25:38,154
那我赢了。
I've won that.

424
00:25:38,227 --> 00:25:39,919
是的，你赢了，赢了。
Yes, you have, you've won.

425
00:25:39,992 --> 00:25:43,786
- 我还想继续。
- 我不管，我不想再跑了。
- I was still going.
- I don't care. I'm not going any more.

426
00:25:43,856 --> 00:25:45,911
我得了埃博拉。
I've got Ebola.

427
00:25:49,919 --> 00:25:52,747
幸好，接下来的测试还能用发动机——
Mercifully, the next test
did involve our engines -

428
00:25:52,817 --> 00:25:55,872
看看哪辆车能冲到最高时速。
which car could achieve
the highest top speed.

429
00:25:57,313 --> 00:25:58,801
他已经到五了。
He's reached five.

430
00:25:59,146 --> 00:26:00,872
颤抖，我已经到80了。
Buffeting, I've got 80.

431
00:26:00,944 --> 00:26:03,135
雷达陷阱已经设好。
The radar trap was set.

432
00:26:04,575 --> 00:26:07,334
90！天呐，装饰件都掉了！
90! Good God, the trim's coming off!

433
00:26:08,173 --> 00:26:13,693
不过装了6.75升V8，最终结果应该相当惊人。
But with a 6.75 liter V8,
the final result should be impressive.

434
00:26:14,769 --> 00:26:16,529
结果却不咋样。
It wasn't.

435
00:26:17,833 --> 00:26:20,854
胎儿都比这出生得快。
Children come out of the womb
faster than that.

436
00:26:20,931 --> 00:26:22,623
我的天！
Oh, my God!

437
00:26:24,496 --> 00:26:29,515
在詹姆斯还没停下来之前，我已经点火了那台6.3升的Big。
Before James had stopped,
I fired up the 6.3 liter Big.

438
00:26:29,592 --> 00:26:34,544
这车在1969年的最高时速是128。
Top speed of this car in 1969 was 128.

439
00:26:36,121 --> 00:26:38,415
120……公里/小时。
120... kph.

440
00:26:38,486 --> 00:26:39,781
130。
130.

441
00:26:41,417 --> 00:26:43,643
160——来了，一百英里每小时！
160 - there it is, 100 miles an hour!

442
00:26:44,881 --> 00:26:45,971
170！
170!

443
00:26:47,279 --> 00:26:49,403
停！
Stop!

444
00:26:51,610 --> 00:26:57,596
我的刹车快着火了，烟都冒出来了。
它根本没停住，现在都燃起来了。
My brakes are on fire. We can see the
smoke. It didn't stop and now it's on fire.

445
00:26:58,638 --> 00:27:00,762
仍然停得更好
比我好，我得承认。
It still stopped better
than me, I have to say.

446
00:27:00,837 --> 00:27:03,301
是啊，你的刹车距离简直烂透。
Yeah, your stopping distance is rubbish.

447
00:27:04,534 --> 00:27:07,124
比分是2比1，戈瑟领跑，
With the score at 2-1 to the Grosser,

448
00:27:07,200 --> 00:27:11,095
我们被给了Top Gear史上最容易的挑战——
we were given the easiest challenge
in the history of Top Gear -

449
00:27:11,163 --> 00:27:14,423
去伦敦市中心找个位子停下。
go to the center of London and park.

450
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:19,352
路上，
我们停下来喝了杯茶，
0n the way,
we stopped for a cup of tea,

451
00:27:19,424 --> 00:27:21,980
还有关于油耗的争论。
and an argument about running costs.

452
00:27:22,056 --> 00:27:26,451
我上次保养账单，212.09英镑。
My last service bill, £212.09.

453
00:27:26,519 --> 00:27:28,983
就是这个。
There it is.

454
00:27:29,051 --> 00:27:33,810
- 212镑买根软管。
- 对。
- £212 for a hosepipe.
- Yes.

455
00:27:33,881 --> 00:27:35,641
你的是多少？
What was yours?

456
00:27:35,714 --> 00:27:38,008
看了哭吧。
这就是最后一次保养账单。
Read it and weep.
That's the last service bill.

457
00:27:39,510 --> 00:27:40,509
呃？
Eh?

458
00:27:41,509 --> 00:27:42,804
五十……
Fifty...

459
00:27:45,074 --> 00:27:48,799
- 我一开始读错了，15000……
- 嗯，那又怎样？
- I misread that at first. 15,000...
- Yeah, and?

460
00:27:48,871 --> 00:27:51,528
915镑
零点五九便士。
Nine hundred and fifteen pounds
and fifty nine pence.

461
00:27:51,602 --> 00:27:54,532
是的，保养花了15900镑。
Yes, £15,900 for a service.

462
00:27:54,600 --> 00:27:57,462
说实在的，维修项目真不少，
老实说。
There was quite a lot needed doing,
if I'm honest.

463
00:27:57,532 --> 00:28:00,893
他到底干了啥，
给你买了辆高尔夫？
What did he do, buy you a Golf?

464
00:28:04,294 --> 00:28:08,746
在伦敦，我们的车显然
比任何别人的都强太多了。
In London, our cars were plainly
so much better than anyone else's.

465
00:28:09,757 --> 00:28:12,982
看看你，
坐在你的宝马后座的样子。
Look at you, look at you
in the back of your Beamer.

466
00:28:13,055 --> 00:28:16,178
像个商人，
根本不是独裁者。
Looks like a businessman,
not a dictator.

467
00:28:16,253 --> 00:28:20,444
看看他活在自己的
董事长玛格丽特·克拉克森的幻想里。
Look at him living out his
Chairman Margaret Clarkson fantasy.

468
00:28:22,448 --> 00:28:23,708
别按喇喇叭，詹姆斯，
Don't blow your horn James,

469
00:28:23,781 --> 00:28:26,711
不然我把我的吹回来，
让你耳朵嗡嗡响。
or I'll blow mine back
and then your ears'll bleed.

470
00:28:27,612 --> 00:28:32,700
当然，我们两万五千镑的车有点
庞大，
Sure, our £25,000 cars were a bit enormous,

471
00:28:32,775 --> 00:28:38,170
不过说到这种级别的豪华，
空间自然要多。
but then you need a lot of space when
you're talking about this level of luxury.

472
00:28:38,238 --> 00:28:40,464
这就是我的鸡尾酒柜。
This is my cocktail cabinet here.

473
00:28:40,536 --> 00:28:42,364
当然，装了空调，
Air-conditioned, of course,

474
00:28:42,435 --> 00:28:44,921
还有专门放烈酒杯的挂架。
with mounting points for your shot glasses.

475
00:28:47,065 --> 00:28:51,892
这里有个有趣的早期安全特性。车窗降下，
车窗升起，
Here's an interesting early safety feature.
Window goes down, window goes up,

476
00:28:51,962 --> 00:28:53,949
但只升到离完全关闭差几英寸，
but stops a couple of inches short,

477
00:28:54,027 --> 00:28:58,820
然后按下小按钮它会把剩余的缝隙关闭——
防止你把手指割掉。
then you press a little button and it closes
- that's so you don't cut your finger off.

478
00:29:04,053 --> 00:29:07,211
看看这公交——他为什么要这么干？
Look at this bus -
why does he have to do that?

479
00:29:08,484 --> 00:29:11,414
你可不会对大多数
600的司机这么干，兄弟。
You wouldn't do that to most
600 drivers, mate.

480
00:29:11,482 --> 00:29:13,673
你就会被扔进后备箱，
脑袋都找不到。
You'd be in the boot without your head.

481
00:29:15,612 --> 00:29:19,473
很快就不需要动手干掉谁，直接来到西区，
Soon though, without executing anyone,
we were in the West End,

482
00:29:19,542 --> 00:29:23,199
我们只要找个地方停下来。会有多难？
and all we had to do was park.
How hard could that be?

483
00:29:24,007 --> 00:29:26,732
不行，双黄线。
No, double yellow lines.

484
00:29:26,804 --> 00:29:30,030
单黄线，双黄线。
Single yellow line, double yellow line.

485
00:29:31,867 --> 00:29:35,389
结果简直噩梦，因为每当我们真的找到车位时，
It turned out to be a nightmare,
because when we did come across a space,

486
00:29:35,465 --> 00:29:38,225
车位里总是被那辆自鸣得意的小车占了。
it always had a smug-mobile in it.

487
00:29:40,428 --> 00:29:41,450
快看看那车！
Look at them!

488
00:29:42,327 --> 00:29:46,154
两个G‑Wiz挤在一个车位，真是自私。
Two G-Wizzes taking up one space,
that's just selfish.

489
00:29:46,224 --> 00:29:49,710
在梅伊的英国，这可要被判六个月监禁。
In May's Britain, that would be punishable
by six months in prison.

490
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:53,309
不过好在，电动车司机一点颜面都没有，
Happily though, electric car drivers
have no style,

491
00:29:53,386 --> 00:29:58,145
于是我们直接奔向唯一肯定没有G‑Wiz的地方。
so we headed for the one place
we knew would be G-Wiz free.

492
00:29:58,216 --> 00:30:03,202
萨维尔街，那里总能找到车位。
Saville Row, there's always a parking space
on Saville Row.

493
00:30:04,679 --> 00:30:07,143
詹姆斯，那是车位，我要占下来。
James, that's a parking space,
I'm gonna have it.

494
00:30:07,211 --> 00:30:10,232
现在我们可以收场了。
Now we could put this challenge to bed.

495
00:30:10,308 --> 00:30:14,204
我会平行停车，我在伦敦住了十八年。
I'm good at parallel parking,
I lived in London for 18 years.

496
00:30:14,272 --> 00:30:15,532
我怎样？
How am I doing?

497
00:30:15,605 --> 00:30:16,627
糟透了。
Badly.

498
00:30:17,670 --> 00:30:21,122
但我一定要停好，哪怕要了我的命。来吧。
But I am gonna park, if it kills me.
Come on.

499
00:30:29,829 --> 00:30:31,316
不行。
No.

500
00:30:31,394 --> 00:30:33,052
你到底想让我干嘛？
What exactly would you like me to do?

501
00:30:33,126 --> 00:30:34,455
啊——！
Aargh!

502
00:30:34,525 --> 00:30:36,455
天啊，太尴尬了。
God, this is embarrassing.

503
00:30:36,523 --> 00:30:40,112
# BBC Radio 2 #
# BBC Radio 2 #

504
00:30:40,188 --> 00:30:43,084
这已经开始影响去哈罗盖特的交通了。
And that's affecting traffic
going into Harrogate.

505
00:30:43,152 --> 00:30:46,048
终于有人打来电话，抱怨严重拥堵和延误
Finally, we're getting calls
about severe congestion and delays

506
00:30:46,117 --> 00:30:48,547
在伦敦市中心摄政街一带。
around Regent Street in central London.

507
00:30:48,616 --> 00:30:51,580
我也不清楚发生了啥，但打电话的人说简直是噩梦，
Don't know what's going on,
but callers are saying it's a nightmare,

508
00:30:51,647 --> 00:30:53,612
所以暂时绕开吧。
so avoid it for the time being.

509
00:30:53,679 --> 00:30:56,199
先说这么多，半小时后会有更多交通新闻。
That's it for now.
More traffic news in around half an hour.

510
00:30:56,277 --> 00:30:57,969
估计装不进去吧？
It's not gonna fit, is it?

511
00:30:58,042 --> 00:31:00,404
于是，我英勇地放弃了。
So, bravely, I gave up.

512
00:31:00,474 --> 00:31:02,336
真的很抱歉。
I'm really sorry about that.

513
00:31:02,406 --> 00:31:03,735
抱歉。
Sorry.

514
00:31:03,805 --> 00:31:05,736
抱歉。抱歉。
Sorry. Sorry.

515
00:31:12,100 --> 00:31:16,461
我不知道普通伦敦车位有多长，
I do not know how long
a standard London parking bay is,

516
00:31:16,530 --> 00:31:23,049
但我猜大概比奔驰大一点儿短一英尺左右。
but I suspect it's about a foot shorter
than the Mercedes Big.

517
00:31:24,691 --> 00:31:28,587
终于，我们找到两个能直接停进去的车位。
Eventually,
we did find two end on spaces.

518
00:31:28,655 --> 00:31:30,210
不过……
However...

519
00:31:30,287 --> 00:31:32,252
钱放哪儿？
Where do you put the money?

520
00:31:33,618 --> 00:31:35,243
只能刷卡。
Cards only.

521
00:31:35,318 --> 00:31:40,474
真是烦人，说明太小了——非常小。
Annoyingly, the instructions were tiny -
very tiny.

522
00:31:40,547 --> 00:31:44,533
因为伦敦说的语言太多，全部都是标志——
Because of all the different languages
spoken in London, it's all just signs -

523
00:31:44,611 --> 00:31:46,576
那标志上的减号/加号到底是干嘛的……
what does that flag minus/plus...

524
00:31:46,642 --> 00:31:50,629
那儿肯定是让你填密码的地方。
That's where you put your pin number,
I'm sure.

525
00:31:50,707 --> 00:31:53,432
- 对。
- 把卡塞回去。
- Right.
- Put your card back in.

526
00:31:53,505 --> 00:31:56,333
“Selectionne avec bouton bleu”？
"Selectionne avec bouton bleu"?

527
00:31:56,403 --> 00:31:57,891
啊，这下应该是……
Ah, now that must...

528
00:31:57,968 --> 00:32:01,126
“Pagmento”？这是什么玩意儿？
"Pagmento"? Where's that from?

529
00:32:02,765 --> 00:32:05,820
- 点所有的东西。
- 你刚把它取消了。
- Hit everything.
- You've just canceled it.

530
00:32:05,896 --> 00:32:07,384
钱到底是怎么回事？
What was the matter with money?

531
00:32:07,461 --> 00:32:11,857
- “把卡拿走”。
- 我们根本没付钱，被拦住了。
- "Remove card."
- We haven't paid, we've been thwarted.

532
00:32:15,157 --> 00:32:18,847
在下一个地点我们发现，不需要信用卡。
At the next place we found,
you didn't need credit cards.

533
00:32:18,921 --> 00:32:21,079
不过……
However...

534
00:32:21,152 --> 00:32:23,708
顾客必须先开个账户。
Customers are required
to set up an account.

535
00:32:23,784 --> 00:32:26,146
需要一张有效的信用卡或借记卡。
You will need a valid credit or debit card.

536
00:32:26,216 --> 00:32:29,577
所有新手机停车交易都有最高限额……
All new phone park transactions
are subject to a max...

537
00:32:29,647 --> 00:32:33,042
你得负责填对车辆位置……
You are responsible for entering
the correct vehicle location...

538
00:32:33,111 --> 00:32:36,132
我们网络的停车法规……
parking regulation
of our network delivery...

539
00:32:36,209 --> 00:32:39,934
或在必要时找其他车位。
or find an alternative space
where necessary.

540
00:32:48,600 --> 00:32:51,496
- 我们已经在这儿多久了？
- 我这辈子都在这儿。
- How long have we been now?
- All my life.

541
00:32:52,964 --> 00:32:54,622
我们英勇地再次放弃了，
Bravely, we gave up again,

542
00:32:54,696 --> 00:32:58,421
然后冲向传统的多层停车场。
and headed for a traditional multistory.

543
00:32:58,494 --> 00:33:01,685
瞧——一张停车票。
Look at that - a ticket to park a car.

544
00:33:03,657 --> 00:33:05,088
这玩意儿太棒了——
This was great -

545
00:33:05,155 --> 00:33:08,551
他们不管怎么收钱，给你的就是车位。
they take your money however it comes
and in return, you get spaces.

546
00:33:09,653 --> 00:33:11,515
对！
Yes!

547
00:33:11,585 --> 00:33:14,140
我进来了，已经停好。
I am in, I'm parked.

548
00:33:15,215 --> 00:33:16,510
啊！
Ah!

549
00:33:19,846 --> 00:33:21,776
噢，不。
Oh, no.

550
00:33:22,844 --> 00:33:24,808
我出不来。
I can't get out.

551
00:33:24,876 --> 00:33:27,000
詹姆斯也进不去。
And James couldn't get in.

552
00:33:27,075 --> 00:33:29,164
根本塞不进去。
It doesn't fit.

553
00:33:29,240 --> 00:33:32,499
这把所有人都气得不行。
Which was making everyone very cross.

554
00:33:32,570 --> 00:33:34,467
闭嘴。
Shut up.

555
00:33:34,536 --> 00:33:37,295
好吧，你想搞喇叭赛——
OK, fine, you wanna have a horn race -

556
00:33:37,367 --> 00:33:39,389
准备，预备……
ready, steady...

557
00:33:45,395 --> 00:33:46,984
这才是真正的喇叭。
Now, that's a horn.

558
00:33:47,361 --> 00:33:50,052
结果我们被赶出了。
And it got us thrown out.

559
00:33:51,224 --> 00:33:56,619
看来大车司机在伦敦已经不可能停下来。
It was becoming apparent that the large car
driver cannot stop in London any more.

560
00:33:56,687 --> 00:33:59,708
而且现在加油站少得可怜，
And because there are now
so few petrol stations,

561
00:33:59,786 --> 00:34:03,080
继续下去也实在是太艰难了。
it is also extremely
difficult to keep going.

562
00:34:04,116 --> 00:34:06,080
哎呀，见鬼！
Oh, bloody hell!

563
00:34:06,148 --> 00:34:07,976
杰兹，我油没了。
Jezza, I've run out.

564
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:09,772
稍等，我过去帮你一把。
Hang on, I'll come and give you a hand.

565
00:34:09,845 --> 00:34:14,104
在普通车里，这不丢人。但…
In a normal car, this is not embarrassing.
However...

566
00:34:19,706 --> 00:34:21,932
杰兹，救命！救命，救命！
Jezza, help. Help, help!

567
00:34:24,436 --> 00:34:27,457
我要被…要被强奸之类的。
I'm gonna get...
I'm gonna get raped or something.

568
00:34:28,866 --> 00:34:31,796
- 来吧，兄弟，打方向盘。  
- 用脚踩到底。
- Come on, man, turn the wheel.
- Put your foot down.

569
00:34:31,864 --> 00:34:33,795
稳住。
Hang on.

570
00:34:33,863 --> 00:34:36,350
来啊，詹姆斯，加油！
Come on, James, pump it!

571
00:34:38,559 --> 00:34:40,421
这可是他有史以来最快的速度。
That's the fastest he's ever been.

572
00:34:40,492 --> 00:34:43,115
还有谁在偷懒？
Anybody not doing anything?

573
00:34:43,189 --> 00:34:47,209
伦敦，这座城市太棒了，
London. It is a fantastic city,

574
00:34:47,286 --> 00:34:54,204
但很不幸的是，要是开像詹姆斯那种车，就再也去不了。
but unfortunately, if you have a car like
James', you can't go there any more.

575
00:34:55,714 --> 00:34:57,940
- 哦，已经塞到嘴里了？  
- 是的，塞进去了。
- Oh, has it gone in your mouth?
- Yes, it has.

576
00:34:58,012 --> 00:35:01,033
承认吧，我的车更牛逼。
Just admit that mine's the superior car.

577
00:35:02,243 --> 00:35:04,673
它油箱容量更大，这点我得承认。
It's got more petrol in
it, I will admit that.

578
00:35:12,369 --> 00:35:15,231
颜色跟胎盘一样。
It's the color of an afterbirth.

579
00:35:17,466 --> 00:35:21,055
这事只能这么了结。
There is only one way we can settle this.

580
00:35:21,130 --> 00:35:23,856
所以，我这里有一份名人名单，
So, what I've got here
is a list of famous people,

581
00:35:23,929 --> 00:35:26,825
过去曾拥有一辆配有镀铬前脸的福特Zephyr的。
who, in the past, have owned a Ford Zephyr
with a chrome nose.

582
00:35:29,225 --> 00:35:31,485
记得吗？“哎呀，你太烂了，但我喜欢你。”
Remember? "Ooh, you are
awful, but I like you."

583
00:35:31,557 --> 00:35:32,852
还有詹姆斯·梅。
And James May.

584
00:35:33,488 --> 00:35:36,577
他们有什么共同点？呃…
What do they all have in common? Erm...

585
00:35:36,653 --> 00:35:39,549
你想说的是，因为我有一辆康纳奇，
What you're trying to say is,
that because I've got a Corniche,

586
00:35:39,617 --> 00:35:44,672
所以我必定衣橱里全是亮闪闪的连体衣。
I must, by association,
have a wardrobe full of spangly jumpsuits.

587
00:35:44,748 --> 00:35:48,370
- 对，就是啊，闪亮连体衣哥！  
- 行，好吧，算了。
- That's it, yes, spangly jumpsuit man!
- Right, OK, fair enough.

588
00:35:48,445 --> 00:35:51,807
好吧。我们来看看这车的前任大老板们是谁——他们是…
Fair enough. Let's have a look at the Bigs
famous former owners - they are...

589
00:35:51,876 --> 00:35:53,170
名单上有马克斯·莫斯利吗？
Is Max Mosley on that list?

590
00:35:53,241 --> 00:35:54,467
没有。
No.

591
00:35:54,541 --> 00:35:56,563
更糟了，更糟了。
It's worse, it's worse.

592
00:36:05,300 --> 00:36:07,322
这名单真够气派的。
An impressive list.

593
00:36:07,398 --> 00:36:10,419
名单确实气派，但如果你的理论成立，
It is an impressive list,
but if your theory is correct,

594
00:36:10,496 --> 00:36:12,756
那就意味着你要灭掉数百万人，
that means you're gonna murder
millions of people,

595
00:36:12,828 --> 00:36:16,815
或者在马桶里死去，只为把五百个芝士汉堡从粪便管里弄出来。
or die on the bog trying to get
500 cheeseburgers out of your poo chute.

596
00:36:21,356 --> 00:36:23,877
所以说，归根结底就是一个简单的选择——
So, really, it comes down
to a simple choice -

597
00:36:23,954 --> 00:36:25,248
露营…
camp...

598
00:36:25,319 --> 00:36:27,284
- 还是营地指挥官。  
- 正是。
- Or camp commandant.
- Exactly.

599
00:36:28,052 --> 00:36:31,981
好了，现在该给我们这辆性价比高的车装点星光了。
Anyway, now it is time to put some stars
in our reasonably priced car.

600
00:36:32,049 --> 00:36:36,910
今晚我的嘉宾都是《天降奇才》里人气极高的两位评委。
Now, my guests tonight are both judges on
the immensely popular show Dragons Den.

601
00:36:36,979 --> 00:36:40,703
我唯一的烦恼是他们其中一个名字，简直是拗口得要死。
The only problem I've got is that one of them
has a name that's very hard to pronounce.

602
00:36:40,776 --> 00:36:42,435
好了，各位女士们先生们，事儿要开始了，
So, here we go, ladies and gentlemen,

603
00:36:42,508 --> 00:36:46,131
请欢迎 Theodorus Paphitis 和 Peter……哎呀，见鬼！
please welcome Theodorus Paphitis
and Peter... Oh, damn it!

604
00:36:46,205 --> 00:36:49,999
Jo……Jon……高个儿的，那位！
Jo... Jon... The taller one, yeah!

605
00:36:56,365 --> 00:36:58,227
坐下吧。
Have a seat.

606
00:37:01,095 --> 00:37:02,787
好了……
Now...

607
00:37:02,861 --> 00:37:07,586
首先我要聊的就是——自从我们每周请两位嘉宾后，
What I want to talk about first of all is this
- since we started having two guests a week,

608
00:37:07,658 --> 00:37:10,622
本来以为每周的沙发上会来点竞争的味道，
we thought it would be a competition
on the sofa every week,

609
00:37:10,689 --> 00:37:14,312
但每周大家都客气得要命，‘啊不，我肯定比你快’。
but every week everyone comes over so polite
"Oh, no, I'm sure you'll be faster than me."

610
00:37:14,387 --> 00:37:16,476
‘啊不，真的，我肯定会的’。
"Oh, no, really, I'm sure you will be."

611
00:37:16,551 --> 00:37:19,344
我倒是看得出你们俩根本不会这么说。
I'm getting the impression
you two won't be like that.

612
00:37:19,416 --> 00:37:20,642
绝对不会。
Absolutely not.

613
00:37:20,715 --> 00:37:22,339
我们还有几个问题要问你们。
We've got some questions to ask you.

614
00:37:23,647 --> 00:37:25,237
到底是哪些？
What are they?

615
00:37:25,312 --> 00:37:28,935
明明在赛道上玩了那么久，怎么就开不快了？
Why is it that you can't drive fast after all
the experience you've had on that track?

616
00:37:31,175 --> 00:37:34,434
我弱得要命，软弱盲目，毫无希望，还吓得要死。
I'm weak, feeble, blind,
hopeless and terrified.

617
00:37:34,506 --> 00:37:37,470
我们以后再看看你们的成绩吧？
Shall we find out your times later on?

618
00:37:37,537 --> 00:37:39,195
- 不。  
- 现在来吧。
- No.
- Now, please.

619
00:37:39,269 --> 00:37:42,062
- 稍后吧。  
- 我已经给你多加了十秒。
No, later on.
I've just added ten seconds to yours.

620
00:37:42,434 --> 00:37:44,490
哦，是啊！
Oh, yes!

621
00:37:44,566 --> 00:37:47,757
你们看，他们已经把比赛启动了。
You see, they've already started
with the competition.

622
00:37:47,830 --> 00:37:51,316
听着，商业里，赢是不是几乎等于一切？
Listen, in business,
is winning kind of everything?

623
00:37:51,395 --> 00:37:53,791
不是，一切不都是赢。
No, it's not everything.

624
00:37:53,860 --> 00:37:55,086
还有别的东西吗？
What else is there?

625
00:37:55,159 --> 00:37:57,952
这不就是一切吗？
It is everything, isn't it?

626
00:37:58,024 --> 00:38:00,386
- 对，这就是一切。  
- 他在撒谎。
- Yeah, it is everything.
- He's lying.

627
00:38:00,455 --> 00:38:01,942
对，这就是一切。
Yeah, it is everything.

628
00:38:02,021 --> 00:38:04,212
而你们的评价标准就是赚了多少现金。
And you judge it
on how much cash you make.

629
00:38:04,286 --> 00:38:08,841
这只是一张记分卡——钱只是记分卡之一，算是副产品罢了。
It's just a score card - the cash
is a score card. It's a by-product.

630
00:38:08,917 --> 00:38:11,346
它会说，你有好年，也有烂年。
It says, you've had a good year,
you've had a bad year.

631
00:38:11,414 --> 00:38:14,378
你们是干什么的？订书机？
Yours is what?
You do stapling machines.

632
00:38:14,445 --> 00:38:16,807
我经营小店——内衣、胸罩、文具……
I'm a shopkeeper -
knickers, bras, stationery...

633
00:38:16,877 --> 00:38:20,500
- 我以为你把内裤都卖掉了。  
- 我留了一点，免得手痒。
- I thought you got rid of the knickers.
- I kept a bit just to keep my hand in.

634
00:38:22,540 --> 00:38:24,504
所以，你会看看《星期日泰晤士报》的富豪榜，
So, do you look at the
Sunday Times rich list,

635
00:38:24,572 --> 00:38:27,332
然后盯着它想‘他比我强’吗？
and you have to look at him and think
"He's ahead of me"?

636
00:38:27,403 --> 00:38:28,834
不，根本是玩儿的。
Nah, cos it's rubbish.

637
00:38:28,903 --> 00:38:31,060
- 哦，你真的在看！  
- 没有，我没看。
- Oh, you do, you do!
- I don't. I don't.

638
00:38:31,134 --> 00:38:33,156
- 你在看。  
- 我不看。
- You do.
- I don't.

639
00:38:33,233 --> 00:38:34,061
真的，你在看。
You do, seriously.

640
00:38:34,132 --> 00:38:37,187
每个星期天，杰里米，报纸一出来，我就收到那条小信息，
Every Sunday, Jeremy, when it comes out,
I get that little text,

641
00:38:37,264 --> 00:38:39,694
它通常会这么说
and it normally says

642
00:38:42,094 --> 00:38:44,081
你们竟然还能在身高上竞争。
You even compete on height.

643
00:38:44,158 --> 00:38:45,316
不，我们不这么玩。
No, we don't.

644
00:38:45,391 --> 00:38:48,719
- 不，西奥已经不玩这个了，我想。
- 他个子高。
- No, Theo's given up on that one, I think.
- He is tall.

645
00:38:48,789 --> 00:38:50,650
你还嘲笑他个子小。
You mock him for his smallness.

646
00:38:50,721 --> 00:38:54,151
我唯一嘲讽他的，就是我们有这些迈巴赫时，
The only thing I mock him about
is that when we had these Maybachs,

647
00:38:54,218 --> 00:38:56,240
他买的比我那辆稍微长一点，
he bought a slightly longer one than mine,

648
00:38:56,317 --> 00:39:00,042
而且他还把车窗全弄成黑的。那点我真的不懂，西奥啊。
and he also blacked out his windows. That's
the bit I really don't get with Theo.

649
00:39:00,114 --> 00:39:02,204
你怎么会买一辆跟迈巴赫一样大的车，
Why would you buy a car
the size of a Maybach,

650
00:39:02,280 --> 00:39:05,108
然后在你这么个四尺矮子身上把窗户全弄黑？
then black out your windows
when you're four foot nothing?

651
00:39:06,510 --> 00:39:09,303
他根本看不见你在里头怎么想。
He's never gonna see you looking in anyway.

652
00:39:09,375 --> 00:39:13,100
你把高个子这个概念套上去，挺好，却把它毁了，
You've taken the idea of tallness,
which is good, and sort of ruined it,

653
00:39:13,173 --> 00:39:14,831
因为你已经玩脱了。
cos you've gone over the top.

654
00:39:14,905 --> 00:39:17,528
- 你真的这么做了。
- 看看他的脚！
- You have really.
- Look at his feet!

655
00:39:17,603 --> 00:39:21,760
看看他的袜子。到底是什么鬼把它们穿上去的？
Look at his socks.
What possessed you to put those?

656
00:39:21,833 --> 00:39:22,957
码数是14号。
Size 14s.

657
00:39:23,032 --> 00:39:27,825
- 不！
- 你根本不用租滑雪板就能去滑雪。
- No!
- You could go skiing without renting any skis.

658
00:39:29,628 --> 00:39:32,990
这么高也没啥用。直接告诉他这太荒唐了就行。
There's no point being that tall.
You can just tell him it's ridiculous.

659
00:39:33,059 --> 00:39:37,113
我只是想把话题转回去，因为你提到了迈巴赫。
I just want to get onto this business,
cos you brought it up, the Maybachs.

660
00:39:37,190 --> 00:39:38,246
看，那儿，瞧瞧。
There it is, look.

661
00:39:38,322 --> 00:39:41,286
不明智啊，伙计们，极其不明智。
Unwise, gentlemen, very, very unwise.

662
00:39:41,354 --> 00:39:42,909
史上最佳座驾。
Best car ever.

663
00:39:42,986 --> 00:39:44,507
不，它根本不是，差得远呢。
No, it isn't, not even close.

664
00:39:44,584 --> 00:39:49,411
我试驾过幻影。我的船都比那幻影稳。
I had a Phantom on trial.
My boat is more stable than that Phantom.

665
00:39:49,481 --> 00:39:53,206
我以前有辆莫里斯·马里纳——比幻影还稳。
I used to have a Morris Marina -
that was more stable than the Phantom.

666
00:39:53,279 --> 00:39:56,243
你有辆莫里斯·马里纳——这解释了你怎么会买迈巴赫。
You had a Morris Marina -
that explains why you've bought a Maybach.

667
00:39:56,309 --> 00:39:57,468
没错。
Exactly.

668
00:39:57,542 --> 00:40:00,439
老实说，我曾经坐在后排开过那种车，
Honestly, I once drove in one of those,
sitting in the back,

669
00:40:00,507 --> 00:40:03,233
路过公交站那帮东欧建筑工人。
past some Eastern European builders
at a bus stop.

670
00:40:04,338 --> 00:40:07,359
它让我重新定义了恨的含义。
It redefined for me what hate is.

671
00:40:08,702 --> 00:40:13,687
这不过是一辆600日内瓦的出租车，后座铺了点绸缎。
It's just a 600 Geneva taxi
with a bit of chintz in the back.

672
00:40:13,764 --> 00:40:15,490
- 你见过他的颜色吗？
- 见过。
- Have you seen the color of his?
- I have.

673
00:40:15,563 --> 00:40:18,493
前几天我在伦敦的邦德街走着——
I was walking down Bond Street
the other day in London -

674
00:40:18,561 --> 00:40:19,890
它是米色的，伙计。
it's beige, mate.

675
00:40:19,961 --> 00:40:22,516
那就是犹太赛车金色。
That's Jewish racing gold.

676
00:40:25,090 --> 00:40:29,042
有件事我真在意，你们都有孩子——
There's one thing I am really
interested in, you've all got kids -

677
00:40:29,121 --> 00:40:31,279
如果你们真的赚了大钱，
if you make really a lot of money,

678
00:40:31,353 --> 00:40:34,283
对孩子们有个不错的想法，不是吗？
you've got quite a good idea for your kids,
haven't you?

679
00:40:34,350 --> 00:40:37,837
我想，因为，我在想‘当你赚到大钱时，你会怎么做，
I thought because, I thought "What do you
do when you are making a lot of money,

680
00:40:37,914 --> 00:40:40,845
而且你真的想让孩子们脚踏实地。'
"and you really want your kids
to be as grounded as possible."

681
00:40:40,912 --> 00:40:42,843
现在，你知道那根本不可能发生，
Now, you know that's
not really gonna happen,

682
00:40:42,911 --> 00:40:45,739
因为迟早他们会尝到你劳动的果实，
insofar as they'll have
the fruits of your labor at some point,

683
00:40:45,809 --> 00:40:49,001
于是我决定……其实，我设立了一个信托基金。
So I decided...
Actually, I set up a trust fund.

684
00:40:49,074 --> 00:40:51,334
当他们去工作，开始赚钱时，
When they go to work
and start to earn money,

685
00:40:51,406 --> 00:40:55,358
他们一年赚的每一笔钱，信托基金都会翻倍给他们。
for every amount of money they earn in one
year, the trust fund pays them double.

686
00:40:55,436 --> 00:40:59,161
所以，与其一次性拿到一千万、一百万、甚至十万英镑，
So, rather than getting ten million pounds
or one million pounds, or £100,000,

687
00:40:59,234 --> 00:41:01,698
一次性揽下来随意挥霍，信托基金会直接翻倍。
one lump sum,
that they can just blow to the wind,

688
00:41:01,765 --> 00:41:03,525
信托里还有一条，是鼓励他们做点好事，
the trust fund doubles.

689
00:41:03,597 --> 00:41:07,686
比如去当护士，虽然收入不高，之类的，
Then the other bit in the trust fund is, to
encourage them to do things that are good,

690
00:41:07,761 --> 00:41:11,316
那部分金额会翻三倍甚至四倍。
become a nurse, which isn't well paid,
all those sort of things,

691
00:41:11,392 --> 00:41:13,357
看看，我觉得这主意挺赞的。
then it triples or quadruples.

692
00:41:13,424 --> 00:41:15,252
要是你已经很有钱，却不懂死后该干嘛，我觉得这招挺聪明。
See, I think that's quite a good idea.

693
00:41:15,323 --> 00:41:19,514
好吧，我想聊聊车，行不行？
If you're wealthy and you don't know what to
do when you die, I think that's very clever.

694
00:41:19,586 --> 00:41:21,380
你们俩明明开着迈巴赫，却还是死磕汽油车。
I want to talk about cars, if I may, OK?

695
00:41:21,452 --> 00:41:24,973
你们起步都是Alfasud。
You are both big petrol heads
despite the Maybachs.

696
00:41:25,049 --> 00:41:27,570
- 我们今天才知道的。  
- 真的？
You both started out with Alfasuds.

697
00:41:27,648 --> 00:41:29,545
- 他们刚跟我们说。  
- 我有三辆。
- Which we only found out today.
- Really?

698
00:41:29,613 --> 00:41:31,804
你居然有三辆Alfasud？
- They just told us.
- I had three.

699
00:41:31,878 --> 00:41:33,036
那我就醒悟了。
You had three Alfasuds?

700
00:41:33,111 --> 00:41:34,439
我超爱我的Alfasud。那车子亮橙色的，
Then I got wise.

701
00:41:34,509 --> 00:41:37,372
每天我都得这么上下车——
I loved my Alfasud.
My Alfasud was bright orange

702
00:41:37,441 --> 00:41:40,428
像淑女下马一样。这样子是因为，
and every single day
I had to get in and out of it like this -

703
00:41:40,505 --> 00:41:43,628
它们的门槛是纸糊的，
like a lady dismounts a horse. I had to
go like that and the reason for that,

704
00:41:43,703 --> 00:41:46,394
一踩下去，我直接穿过去。
is that they used to
have papier mâché sills,

705
00:41:46,468 --> 00:41:49,194
总之，Alfasud算是结束了，因为你们改玩高尔夫了……
If I put my foot down, I'd go through them.

706
00:41:49,267 --> 00:41:53,855
那辆后面装了摇晃兔子灯的GT‑R。对。
So, anyway, the Alfasuds went,
cos you did the Golf...

707
00:41:53,930 --> 00:41:56,156
他可真有品味。
The GT-R with the wonky rabbits
in the back. Yes.

708
00:41:56,228 --> 00:41:57,886
你有私人定制车牌吗？
He is a man of great taste.

709
00:41:57,960 --> 00:42:01,118
一个也没有。
Have you got a personal registration plate?

710
00:42:01,191 --> 00:42:02,349
你有多少块私人车牌？
Not one, no.

711
00:42:02,424 --> 00:42:05,287
不少啊。
How many personal registration plates
have you got?

712
00:42:06,321 --> 00:42:07,751
那你自己有车牌吗？
Quite a few.

713
00:42:07,820 --> 00:42:10,512
- 我根本不会买私人车牌。  
- 那太扯了，我给他买了一个。
Have you got a personal registration?

714
00:42:10,585 --> 00:42:14,140
- 什么牌？  
- W411KER
- I wouldn't buy a personal plate.
- That is so wrong, cos I bought him one.

715
00:42:14,216 --> 00:42:18,009
所以，Golf GTI，挺好的，
- What was it?
- W411KER

716
00:42:19,678 --> 00:42:21,802
接着你们就跳进了奔驰的靠谱世界。
So, Golf GTi, good,

717
00:42:21,878 --> 00:42:25,273
不不不！我买了人生第一也是唯一一辆保时捷，944。
and then you moved into the sensible world
of the Mercedes.

718
00:42:25,342 --> 00:42:29,771
- 944？  
- 对。
No. No! I got my first
and last Porsche. 944.

719
00:42:29,838 --> 00:42:31,269
- 你玩保时捷？  
- 我玩的是911 SC Targa。
- 944?
- Yeah.

720
00:42:31,338 --> 00:42:34,631
- You did the Porsche?
- I did the 911 SC Targa.
- You did the Porsche?
- I did the 911 SC Targa.

721
00:42:34,702 --> 00:42:36,859
- 颜色？
- 金的。
- Color?
- Gold.

722
00:42:39,965 --> 00:42:41,294
那之后怎么了？
